-- ============================================================
-- VI. MOONLESS VEIL ORDER (幽冥隐宗)
-- ============================================================

update wf_user.my_frames
set
    cultivation_color    = '#3D3D3D',
    cultivation_school   = 'Moonless Veil Order',
    cultivation_identity = 'The Ashen Patriarch',
    cultivation_art      = 'Smoke Shadow Dao of the Patron Assassin',
    cultivation_doctrine = $doc$The Moonless Veil Order begins and ends with Ash Prime. He is not the most dramatic practitioner of the shadow arts - Loki deceives more elegantly, Ivara hunts more patiently, Mirage dazzles more completely. But Ash Prime is the patron saint of the Orokin assassination network, the original smoke and the original silence. Every shinobi-cultivator in the Order traces lineage back to the moment a blade left no witness and a body left no warmth - only ash. His Smoke Screen does not hide him; it erases the evidence that he was ever present. Teleport does not relocate. It conducts a finisher - the Smoke Shadow Dao's fundamental transaction, covering the distance between here and the target's back as a single unbroken motion. Shuriken does not deal damage. It marks - the Patron Assassin's targeting system, designating who has been chosen for the Blade Storm's attention. Blade Storm does not strike. It adjudicates, shadow-clones delivering verdicts across the entire room simultaneously, each clone a copy of the same irrevocable decision. The Ashen Patriarch does not fight. He finalizes.$doc$
where build_title = 'Shadow Monarch';

update wf_user.my_frames
set
    cultivation_color    = '#2A4A6B',
    cultivation_school   = 'Moonless Veil Order',
    cultivation_identity = 'Trickster Lord',
    cultivation_art      = 'Trickster Mirage Dao of the Hundred Decoys',
    cultivation_doctrine = $doc$Loki Prime is the Moonless Veil Order's philosopher. Where Ash Prime is the Patron Assassin and Ivara Prime is the Silent Huntress, Loki Prime is the one who has decided that the most efficient combat doctrine is the one that never requires you to be where the enemy is pointing. His Norse lineage is obvious and unashamed: he is Loki, the Trickster God, the cultivator of the Aesir who understood that the gods who won through cunning outlasted the gods who won through strength. Decoy does not create a distraction. It creates a liability -- something the enemy has to address, which means something that is not you. Invisibility does not hide Loki Prime. It removes him from the enemy's threat assessment entirely, which is a different and more powerful thing. Switch Teleport does not reposition. It redistributes -- the Trickster's fundamental technique: making the enemy's position your position and your position the enemy's problem. Radial Disarm does not remove weapons. It concludes the Hundred Decoys argument: the moment when every enemy in range realizes simultaneously that they have been fighting a set of premises Loki Prime never accepted.$doc$
where build_title = 'Trickster Lord';

update wf_user.my_frames
set
    cultivation_color    = '#7CFFB2',
    cultivation_school   = 'Moonless Veil Order',
    cultivation_identity = 'Prowling Phantom',
    cultivation_art      = 'Midnight Quiver Dao of the Silent Artemis',
    cultivation_doctrine = $doc$Ivara Prime's ability is literally called Artemis Bow. Her visual design references the poison-dart frog -- a creature whose entire survival strategy is to advertise its lethality while remaining completely unreachable. Her cultivation practice is the most patient in the Moonless Veil Order: Prowl, the signature ability, does not just provide invisibility. It provides invisibility plus pickpocket, the Silent Artemis moving through the battlefield as both predator and scavenger, taking what she needs from enemies who never learned she was there. Quiver does not provide utility arrows. It provides tactical theology -- Dashwire for positioning, Cloak for squad concealment, Noise for misdirection, Sleep for the moment when patience has located the optimal shot. Navigator does not guide projectiles. It rides them -- Ivara Prime becoming the arrow, following it through its arc to ensure it arrives exactly where the Silent Artemis intended. Artemis Bow does not fire. It concludes -- the full weight of the Midnight Quiver Dao expressed in a single volley from a cultivator who has been invisible long enough to make every shot count.$doc$
where build_title = 'Prowling Phantom';

update wf_user.my_frames
set
    cultivation_color    = '#FFD23F',
    cultivation_school   = 'Moonless Veil Order',
    cultivation_identity = 'Phantom Queen',
    cultivation_art      = 'Harlequin Eclipse Dao of Mirrored Stagecraft',
    cultivation_doctrine = $doc$Mirage Prime is the Moonless Veil Order's grand illusionist -- the cultivator whose art operates in the space between what the enemy sees and what is actually happening. Her Commedia dell'Arte lineage is precise: she is the Harlequin, the masked performer whose entire theatrical tradition is built around the gap between the character's apparent buffoonery and the performer's absolute technical mastery. Hall of Mirrors does not create clones. It creates a liability calculation that no enemy can correctly complete -- four identical Mirages, each behaving exactly like the real one, and no available method for determining which is which under fire. Eclipse does not toggle between solar damage boost and lunar damage reduction. It conducts the Harlequin Eclipse Dao's central teaching: that the cultivator who has mastered both solar and lunar qi phases has access to a form of adaptability that single-element practitioners never will. Sleight of Hand does not booby-trap pickups. It converts the battlefield's resource economy into an ambush. Prism does not deal damage. It concludes the Mirrored Stagecraft performance -- the moment when the Phantom Queen stops performing and the audience realizes they were never watching a show. They were inside one.$doc$
where build_title = 'Phantom Queen';

update wf_user.my_frames
set
    cultivation_color    = '#7B1F3D',
    cultivation_school   = 'Moonless Veil Order',
    cultivation_identity = 'Lunar Huntress',
    cultivation_art      = 'Blood-Moon Wolfpack Dao of the Severed Heads',
    cultivation_doctrine = $doc$Voruna's cultivation lineage is Lithuanian -- the forest goddess Zvorunna, the hunter-deity of the Baltic tradition who ran with wolves and whose worship predates the Indo-European migrations. What makes Voruna unique in the Moonless Veil Order is that she did not join the wolfpack. She BECAME the wolfpack, fusing her four dead wolves into herself through a Continuity ritual that the Blood-Moon Wolfpack Dao treats as the supreme act of shadow cultivation: the complete dissolution of the boundary between hunter and hunted, between predator and pack. Ulfrun's Descent does not charge. It is a wolf hitting its target -- the singular, total commitment of a predator whose entire evolutionary history has been building toward this moment. Fangs of Raksh does not apply status effects. It applies the wolfpack's accumulated knowledge of where bodies break. Shroud of Dynar does not provide invisibility. It conducts the Dao's central teaching: the moment before the wolf strikes is not absence. It is the most complete form of presence. Lycath's Hunt does not restore health and energy on kills. It pays the wolfpack dividend -- the ancient compact between Voruna and her dead wolves, that every kill feeds them all.$doc$
where build_title = 'Lunar Huntress';

update wf_user.my_frames
set
    cultivation_color    = '#B8E1F0',
    cultivation_school   = 'Moonless Veil Order',
    cultivation_identity = 'Wailing Sound',
    cultivation_art      = 'Wailing Sound Dao of the Sidhe Keening',
    cultivation_doctrine = $doc$Banshee Prime's Irish bean sidhe lineage is not metaphor. The bean sidhe (anglicized banshee) is the death-herald of Gaelic tradition -- the woman whose keening wail announces that someone in the family is about to die. Banshee Prime does not fight enemies. She announces their deaths with acoustic precision and then makes the announcement true. Sonic Boom does not push enemies. It establishes acoustic authority -- the opening declaration that this space now operates on Banshee Prime's sound frequencies. Sonar does not reveal weak points. It conducts a complete acoustic mapping of every target in range, identifying precisely where the bean sidhe's knowledge of anatomy has located the optimal keening frequency. Silence does not mute abilities. It applies the Moonless Veil Order's deepest discipline: that the cultivator who controls what sounds exist in an environment controls what is real in that environment. Sound Quake does not damage. It concludes the Sidhe Keening -- the full acoustic weight of the death-herald expressed as ground-level subsonic devastation, the wail that was always both announcement and cause.$doc$
where build_title = 'Wailing Sound';


-- ============================================================
-- VII. NECROPOLIS DOMINION (黄泉殿)
-- ============================================================

update wf_user.my_frames
set
    cultivation_color    = '#5E2D8C',
    cultivation_school   = 'Necropolis Dominion',
    cultivation_identity = 'The Soul King',
    cultivation_art      = 'Black Shroud Dao of the Soul Reaper',
    cultivation_doctrine = $doc$Nekros Prime is the Necropolis Dominion's patriarch -- the cultivator who established the School's foundational premise that death is not an endpoint but a resource, and that the practitioner who has mastered the Black Shroud Dao has access to every death that has occurred in their vicinity. Soul Punch does not kill. It harvests the soul-residue of living enemies while they still occupy their bodies -- a technique that the Dao describes as the most efficient form of cultivation, because it produces the resource without requiring the death. Terrify does not apply a fear status effect. It conducts a revelation: every enemy in range suddenly understands that Nekros Prime can see them at the soul level, and what the soul level reveals about their survivability is, by all accounts, not encouraging. Desecrate does not loot additional resources from corpses. It processes -- the Soul Reaper's fundamental agricultural practice, ensuring that no death in range produces less than its full yield. Shadows of the Dead does not summon minions. It reinstates -- pulling the soul-residue of fallen enemies back into their bodies and drafting them into the Nekros Prime's Black Shroud economy, the proof that in the Necropolis Dominion, dying in the Soul King's presence is simply a change of employment.$doc$
where build_title = 'The Soul King';

update wf_user.my_frames
set
    cultivation_color    = '#0F1F2E',
    cultivation_school   = 'Necropolis Dominion',
    cultivation_identity = 'Void Walker',
    cultivation_art      = 'Tempestarii Reaper Dao of the Twin Forms',
    cultivation_doctrine = $doc$Sevagoth is the Necropolis Dominion's most structurally complex cultivator because he is, in the most literal sense, two cultivators: the captain who died aboard the ghost-ship Tempestarii, and the Shadow that continued piloting after the captain's death, navigating the dead ship through the void until something brought both of them back into operational status. Grasp of Lohk does not drain. It reaches -- the captain's hand extended from the spectral plane into the material one, pulling energy across the boundary between what is alive and what is not. Gloom does not apply a slow aura. It bleeds reality -- the Tempestarii's influence spreading outward from Sevagoth's position, making the local physics slightly more sympathetic to the dead. His Shadow does not fight separately. It expresses the Twin Forms Dao's central teaching: that the body and the soul are not one thing that separates at death but two things that were always distinct, and the cultivator who has experienced that distinction has access to combat forms that the merely-living cannot reach. Exalted Shadow does not transform. It merges -- the moment when the captain and his Shadow stop operating in parallel and become, briefly, what they were before the Tempestarii went dark.$doc$
where build_title = 'Void Walker';

update wf_user.my_frames
set
    cultivation_color    = '#8B0000',
    cultivation_school   = 'Necropolis Dominion',
    cultivation_identity = 'Spectral Avenger',
    cultivation_art      = 'Faceless Cavalry Dao of the Mirror That Accuses',
    cultivation_doctrine = $doc$Dagath's cultivation lineage is the Irish Dullahan -- the headless horseman who rides to a name, stops, and calls it out, and whoever owns that name dies. But Dagath adds a dimension the Irish tradition does not contain: the Mirror That Accuses, a reflective surface that does not show you what you look like but what you have done. Her cultivation practice is spectral justice, the Necropolis Dominion's most morally specific art -- not generalized death-cultivation but targeted adjudication. Wyrd Scythes do not orbit. They orbit and record -- phantom weapons that remember every enemy they have passed through. Grave Spirit does not provide a death-cheat mechanic. It conducts a negotiation with the boundary between alive and dead: Dagath agrees to keep fighting in exchange for the right to cross back once when she shouldn't be able to. Doom does not apply a debuff. It reads the judgment from the Mirror -- the moment when a target's accumulated actions have been assessed and the verdict has been delivered. Khra's Reign does not deal damage. It executes the Faceless Cavalry Dao's conclusion: the headless rider arriving at the name she was called to, and everything in range learning that they share it.$doc$
where build_title = 'Spectral Avenger';

update wf_user.my_frames
set
    cultivation_color    = '#CFC7B5',
    cultivation_school   = 'Eidolon Bone Sect',
    cultivation_identity = 'The Consumed King',
    cultivation_art      = 'Void Revenant Warden Dao of the Eidolon Bone Sect',
    cultivation_doctrine = $doc$The Eidolon Bone Sect does not recruit - it devours. Revenant Prime was a Tenno who entered the Plains and did not return as himself. The Eidolon took him apart and rebuilt something older. His Mesmer Skin does not protect; it hypnotizes, because predators do not need armor - they need compliance. His Enthrall does not ally; it owns, because a being remade by a Sentient apex does not ask for loyalty. Reave does not dash; it harvests the soul-residue that living things shed when they run. Danse Macabre does not channel. It expresses - the full Eidolon nature that Revenant Prime carries surfacing as a spinning death-broadcast, the proof that the Tenno who entered the Plains was a raw material and what emerged was something the Eidolons consider complete. The Consumed King is the proof that transcendence and violation are the same event seen from different sides. He did not choose the Eidolon Bone Sect. The sect chose what was left of him.$doc$
where build_title = 'The Consumed King';
